Step 1: Read plaintext ("Hello World") and secret key ("MySecretKey") 
Step 2: Convert the key string into byte format and generate Blowfish key 
Step 3: Initialize cipher using Cipher.getInstance("Blowfish") 
Step 4: Set cipher to encryption mode using the secret key 
Step 5: Divide plaintext into 64-bit blocks 
Step 6: Perform key expansion to generate P-array (18 subkeys) and 4 S-boxes 
Step 7: For each block, perform 16 rounds: 
        a) Left = Left XOR P[i] 
        b) Right = F(Left) XOR Right 
        c) Swap Left and Right 
Step 8: After 16 rounds: 
        a) Swap Left and Right 
        b) Right = Right XOR P[17] 
        c) Left = Left XOR P[18] 
Step 9: Combine Left and Right to form encrypted block 
Step 10: Convert encrypted bytes into Base64 format 
Step 11: Display encrypted ciphertext
